 * `nestedProps(props, defaults)` — a props view whose object props are
 * complete at every depth.
 *
 * Vue resolves a prop's default only when the prop is ABSENT: pass
 * `{ wheel: { gain: 2 } }` for a prop whose default is
 * `{ wheel: { gain: 1, follow: 0.1 }, touch: { … } }` and the component
 * receives exactly the object it was passed — `follow` and `touch` are
 * gone. `propsWithDefaults` decides what the default IS and clones it per
 * instance; it cannot reach inside a supplied object, and nothing on the
 * defaults side can.
 *
 * This view completes the supplied object from the defaults, lazily, on
 * read. A read goes to the real props first and falls back to the default
 * subtree only where the supplied object stops, so every read still
 * passes through Vue's props proxy and leaf tracking is untouched: a
 * parent changing `scroll.wheel.gain` re-renders exactly what read it.
